What are EV & HEV Drive Motor Cores?
EV & HEV Drive Motor Cores serve as the fundamental electromagnetic components in electric and hybrid vehicle propulsion systems. These precision-engineered assemblies consist of stators and rotors that efficiently convert electrical energy into mechanical motion. Manufacturers typically construct these cores using advanced materials like high-grade silicon steel or amorphous metals to minimize energy losses while maximizing power density and thermal performance.

